[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186204024 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" "question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" "question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" "question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/id #uuid "272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/math-academy-id "q-257192" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-2,2]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$0.348$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+6 & 8(-1)(0)-1 \\\\ 8(-1)(0)-1 & 4(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)(0)^{2}+6(-1)-0-2 \\\\ 4(-1)^{2}(0)-(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{23}[\\begin{aligned}-31 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.348 \\\\ 0.087\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer/id #uuid "fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.087" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/id #uuid "cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-257191" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-2,0]\\times [-2,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-0.444$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8(-1)+6 & 8(-1)-1 \\\\ 8(-1)-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}8(-1)(-1)+6(-1)-(-1)-2 \\\\ 4(-1)^{2}-(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 0-(-9)\\cdot (-9)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{81}[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.444 \\\\ -1.012\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer/id #uuid "0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.012" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/id #uuid "08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-257195" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+6x-3y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3x-2y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+6x-3y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3x-2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)+6 & 4(-1)-3 \\\\ 4(-1)-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)(-1)+6(-1)-3(-1)+2 \\\\ 2(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-2(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-2)-(-7)\\cdot (-7)}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{53}[\\begin{aligned}43 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.189 \\\\ -0.340\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" "answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer-field/choices ["answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer/id #uuid "734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.189" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer/id #uuid "c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.340" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204508 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-8x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6xy-8x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6(1)-8 \\\\ 6(1)-8 & 6(1)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}+6(1)-8(1)-1 \\\\ 6(1)(1)-8(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 6-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{32}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.125 \\\\ 1.375\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203011 :answer-field/correct "answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer/id #uuid "f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203012 :answer-field/correct "answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer/id #uuid "6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/id #uuid "5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-257198" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[0,\\,1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}10(1)-4 & 10(0)+4(1)+3 \\\\ 10(0)+4(1)+3 & 4(0)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}10(0)(1)-4(0)+2(1)^{2}+3(1) \\\\ 5(0)^{2}+4(0)(1)+3(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 0-7\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ -7 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{49}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -35\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0.286\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" "answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/id #uuid "e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer/id #uuid "358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer/id #uuid "6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.286" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204025 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" "question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" "question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/id #uuid "7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-257208" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,0]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[-0.2,\\,1.2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2xy-4x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy-4x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-2(1.2)-4 & -2(-0.2) \\\\ -2(-0.2) & 6(1.2)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-2(-0.2)(1.2)-4(-0.2) \\\\ 3(1.2)^{2}-(-0.2)^{2}-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-6.4 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 & 7.2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1.28 \\\\ 1.28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-6.4)\\cdot 7.2-0.4\\cdot 0.4}[\\begin{aligned}7.2 & -0.4 \\\\ -0.4 & -6.4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1.28 \\\\ 1.28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{46.24}[\\begin{aligned}8.704 \\\\ -8.704\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.012 \\\\ 1.012\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" "answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/id #uuid "022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer/id #uuid "c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.012" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer/id #uuid "b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.012" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/id #uuid "040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-257222" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{3}-8x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{3}-8y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{3}-8x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{y}^{3}-8y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}12(2)^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12(2)^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(2)^{3}-8(2) \\\\ 4(2)^{3}-8(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}40 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 40\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{40\\cdot 40-0\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}40 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{1\\,600}[\\begin{aligned}640 \\\\ 640\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.6 \\\\ 1.6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" "answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/id #uuid "5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer/id #uuid "17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer/id #uuid "19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204506 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [-2,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,-2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+8x-3y-8) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+8x-3y-8) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(0)+8 & 4(2)-3 \\\\ 4(2)-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(2)(0)+8(2)-3(0)-8 \\\\ 2(2)^{2}-3(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{8\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.6 \\\\ -0.96\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203008 :answer-field/correct "answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer/id #uuid "cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203009 :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer/id #uuid "c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.960" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204507 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-6,-3]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-6,\\,1]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[-3,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$1.75$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{y}^{2}-6) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+12{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{2}-6) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+12{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4(2) \\\\ 4(2) & 4(-3)+24(2)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(2)^{2}-6 \\\\ 4(-3)(2)+12(2)^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 36\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 36-8\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}36 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{64}[\\begin{aligned}-120 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4.875 \\\\ 1.75\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203010 :answer-field/correct "answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer/id #uuid "e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.875" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/id #uuid "11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/math-academy-id "q-257248" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[2,3]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2.25,\\,1.5]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$1.417$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-6) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6(2.25)-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6(1.5)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3(2.25)^{2}-6(2.25) \\\\ 3(1.5)^{2}-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}7.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{7.5\\cdot 9-0\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7.5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{67.5}[\\begin{aligned}15.1875 \\\\ 5.625\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}2.025 \\\\ 1.417\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/id #uuid "ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204026 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" "question-ce47ce1b-5e64-5fb8-88b0-27f2349480f8" "question-d0e5e71c-da68-5727-a150-890764f120a1" "question-4033d90f-6820-5b6e-97e2-e268a68a992f" "question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/id #uuid "e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/math-academy-id "q-257213" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [-1,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,-1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-5$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-0.524$\n </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy-2x+3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy-2x+3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10(-1)-2 \\\\ 10(-1)-2 & 10(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}5(-1)^{2}-2(-1)-2(1) \\\\ 10(1)(-1)-2(1)+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 10\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-29/82 \\\\ 39/82\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.646 \\\\ -0.524\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" "answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" "answer-field-c7ba4597-ac27-5690-bf79-d5368cab1239" "answer-field-c3d09404-adf2-557f-9a06-f5a9863cc8b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/id #uuid "a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer/id #uuid "7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7ba4597-ac27-5690-bf79-d5368cab1239" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ba4597-ac27-5690-bf79-d5368cab1239" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-684dfc30-4dab-50da-adfc-01aa883edaa6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-684dfc30-4dab-50da-adfc-01aa883edaa6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-684dfc30-4dab-50da-adfc-01aa883edaa6" :answer/id #uuid "684dfc30-4dab-50da-adfc-01aa883edaa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3d09404-adf2-557f-9a06-f5a9863cc8b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3d09404-adf2-557f-9a06-f5a9863cc8b7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-552ba9b1-300d-5b6c-941f-998b43f13bfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-552ba9b1-300d-5b6c-941f-998b43f13bfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-552ba9b1-300d-5b6c-941f-998b43f13bfd" :answer/id #uuid "552ba9b1-300d-5b6c-941f-998b43f13bfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.646" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce47ce1b-5e64-5fb8-88b0-27f2349480f8" :question/id #uuid "ce47ce1b-5e64-5fb8-88b0-27f2349480f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-257214" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-6xy+2x.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[0,\\,1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$6$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-2$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$6$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6x{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-6xy+2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6x{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-6xy+2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(12xy-6x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(12xy-6x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12(1)-6 \\\\ 12(1)-6 & 12(0)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}6(1)^{2}-6(0)-6(1)+2 \\\\ 12(0)(1)-6(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1/3\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0.667\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" "answer-field-d1f5f30c-549c-5b34-abb8-940275af359d" "answer-field-bfb717c0-13de-5925-8e9a-3605309732dc" "answer-field-f29ded99-6e42-55a8-9e12-efe44e59e72b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" :answer-field/id #uuid "4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae" :answer/id #uuid "00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1f5f30c-549c-5b34-abb8-940275af359d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1f5f30c-549c-5b34-abb8-940275af359d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ce8de537-983e-5c76-847d-0ef82aa8faa8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce8de537-983e-5c76-847d-0ef82aa8faa8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce8de537-983e-5c76-847d-0ef82aa8faa8" :answer/id #uuid "ce8de537-983e-5c76-847d-0ef82aa8faa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bfb717c0-13de-5925-8e9a-3605309732dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb717c0-13de-5925-8e9a-3605309732dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e3e6c084-0078-55f2-a9b5-7b352c3ed7c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3e6c084-0078-55f2-a9b5-7b352c3ed7c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3e6c084-0078-55f2-a9b5-7b352c3ed7c6" :answer/id #uuid "e3e6c084-0078-55f2-a9b5-7b352c3ed7c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f29ded99-6e42-55a8-9e12-efe44e59e72b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f29ded99-6e42-55a8-9e12-efe44e59e72b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5d4c5fbe-8fba-5289-91bc-1a6d34117d6e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d4c5fbe-8fba-5289-91bc-1a6d34117d6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d4c5fbe-8fba-5289-91bc-1a6d34117d6e" :answer/id #uuid "5d4c5fbe-8fba-5289-91bc-1a6d34117d6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.667" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0e5e71c-da68-5727-a150-890764f120a1" :question/id #uuid "d0e5e71c-da68-5727-a150-890764f120a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-257201" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=4x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-6xy-x.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,2]^{T}.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$-9$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-6xy-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-6xy-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6x-6y-1 \\\\ 8xy-6x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{2}+6x-6y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy-6x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{y}^{2}+6x-6y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy-6x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8y-6 \\\\ 8y-6 & 8x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8y-6 \\\\ 8y-6 & 8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6x-6y-1 \\\\ 8xy-6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8y-6 \\\\ 8y-6 & 8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6x-6y-1 \\\\ 8xy-6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & 8(2)-6 \\\\ 8(2)-6 & 8(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}4(2)^{2}+6(1)-6(2)-1 \\\\ 8(1)(2)-6(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 8\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d16c318b-433e-5219-bbac-c0dceacd735f" "answer-field-65b0c455-67d2-5558-afa0-2900b8085ad6" "answer-field-002ec56f-2448-5134-85e4-8cbe3fa3a022"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d16c318b-433e-5219-bbac-c0dceacd735f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d16c318b-433e-5219-bbac-c0dceacd735f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d355a1ab-4760-5da8-81c8-ff82042eba6d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d355a1ab-4760-5da8-81c8-ff82042eba6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d355a1ab-4760-5da8-81c8-ff82042eba6d" :answer/id #uuid "d355a1ab-4760-5da8-81c8-ff82042eba6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65b0c455-67d2-5558-afa0-2900b8085ad6" :answer-field/id #uuid "65b0c455-67d2-5558-afa0-2900b8085ad6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-87cb53ab-6033-5d2e-a880-f4c5d0d8a4db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87cb53ab-6033-5d2e-a880-f4c5d0d8a4db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87cb53ab-6033-5d2e-a880-f4c5d0d8a4db" :answer/id #uuid "87cb53ab-6033-5d2e-a880-f4c5d0d8a4db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-002ec56f-2448-5134-85e4-8cbe3fa3a022" :answer-field/id #uuid "002ec56f-2448-5134-85e4-8cbe3fa3a022" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d1cb510-1818-547a-8900-e0080154ff41" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d1cb510-1818-547a-8900-e0080154ff41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d1cb510-1818-547a-8900-e0080154ff41" :answer/id #uuid "2d1cb510-1818-547a-8900-e0080154ff41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4033d90f-6820-5b6e-97e2-e268a68a992f" :question/id #uuid "4033d90f-6820-5b6e-97e2-e268a68a992f" :question/math-academy-id "q-257215" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,0]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}-xy+x-y.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[-1,\\,1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-5$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-1$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-5$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$-0.510$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}-xy+x-y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}-xy+x-y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-y+1 \\\\ -4xy-x-1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-y+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4xy-x-1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-y+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4xy-x-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6x & -4y-1 \\\\ -4y-1 & -4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}6x & -4y-1 \\\\ -4y-1 & -4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-y+1 \\\\ -4xy-x-1\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}6x & -4y-1 \\\\ -4y-1 & -4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-y+1 \\\\ -4xy-x-1\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6(-1) & -4(1)-1 \\\\ -4(1)-1 & -4(-1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}-2(1)^{2}-1+1 \\\\ -4(-1)(1)-(-1)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}24/49 \\\\ -19/49\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{24}{49} \\\\ -\\frac{19}{49}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{24}{49} \\\\ -\\frac{19}{49}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.510 \\\\ 0.612\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1efb643c-734b-58b8-990d-a15c076650e6" "answer-field-51ef4741-c3ce-5d22-a88d-9e3bfc963ad1" "answer-field-a8074289-ced7-55df-b16d-486ca5eaf823" "answer-field-9a9a83ee-ac72-544e-a5b3-d25e821ddf5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1efb643c-734b-58b8-990d-a15c076650e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1efb643c-734b-58b8-990d-a15c076650e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0b968de3-48ac-5509-bda5-bdd182bb0096" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b968de3-48ac-5509-bda5-bdd182bb0096"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b968de3-48ac-5509-bda5-bdd182bb0096" :answer/id #uuid "0b968de3-48ac-5509-bda5-bdd182bb0096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51ef4741-c3ce-5d22-a88d-9e3bfc963ad1" :answer-field/id #uuid "51ef4741-c3ce-5d22-a88d-9e3bfc963ad1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c5cde4ac-83ff-571c-bb29-6811f5eb0038" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5cde4ac-83ff-571c-bb29-6811f5eb0038"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5cde4ac-83ff-571c-bb29-6811f5eb0038" :answer/id #uuid "c5cde4ac-83ff-571c-bb29-6811f5eb0038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8074289-ced7-55df-b16d-486ca5eaf823" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8074289-ced7-55df-b16d-486ca5eaf823" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-60130157-f623-5097-835c-7ab98079c34b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60130157-f623-5097-835c-7ab98079c34b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60130157-f623-5097-835c-7ab98079c34b" :answer/id #uuid "60130157-f623-5097-835c-7ab98079c34b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a9a83ee-ac72-544e-a5b3-d25e821ddf5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9a83ee-ac72-544e-a5b3-d25e821ddf5c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8f020a22-0c34-5fb9-b34e-9967438d2085" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f020a22-0c34-5fb9-b34e-9967438d2085"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f020a22-0c34-5fb9-b34e-9967438d2085" :answer/id #uuid "8f020a22-0c34-5fb9-b34e-9967438d2085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.612" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/id #uuid "5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-257199" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[2,\\,1]^{T}.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$4$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-4$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-2$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-2-4y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-2-4y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4(1) & 4(2) \\\\ 4(2) & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}4(2)(1)-4 \\\\ 2(2)^{2}-2-4(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" "answer-field-f939bf4e-3667-591e-a976-8f0a98ca8d20" "answer-field-60d198fc-19c4-5f13-9019-6484adf07ee3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer/id #uuid "4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f939bf4e-3667-591e-a976-8f0a98ca8d20" :answer-field/id #uuid "f939bf4e-3667-591e-a976-8f0a98ca8d20" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a2f27189-6b5e-525a-89f5-ab63d4ef4e15" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2f27189-6b5e-525a-89f5-ab63d4ef4e15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f27189-6b5e-525a-89f5-ab63d4ef4e15" :answer/id #uuid "a2f27189-6b5e-525a-89f5-ab63d4ef4e15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60d198fc-19c4-5f13-9019-6484adf07ee3" :answer-field/id #uuid "60d198fc-19c4-5f13-9019-6484adf07ee3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-71cba5d6-193f-5c83-907f-4c9e1d767447" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71cba5d6-193f-5c83-907f-4c9e1d767447"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71cba5d6-193f-5c83-907f-4c9e1d767447" :answer/id #uuid "71cba5d6-193f-5c83-907f-4c9e1d767447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205204 :tutorial/content "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,2]\\times[0,2] \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y) =x^2y-2xy^2+x^3-4x.\n$$\n\nLet’s calculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson method, starting at the point $\\mathbf x_0 = \\big[1, \\: 1 \\big]^T.$ \n\nThe Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f : \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_{n+1} = \\mathbf{x}_n - [H_f(\\mathbf{x}_n)]^{-1} \\nabla{f}(\\mathbf{x}_n),\n$$\n\nwhere $H_f(\\mathbf{x}_n)$ and $\\nabla{f}(\\mathbf{x}_n)$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at $\\mathbf{x}_n.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}-4x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}-4x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4xy\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-4xy) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-4xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2y+6x & 2x-4y \\\\ 2x-4y & -4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n![](images/1a/1aa9927e77d85df3630dd9b77e06843a07e0c924122960026aadfd21c91f416b.svg)\n\nStarting with\n![](images/d7/d7718312d2d119ae3553809c1efd8e253d0aecc8b0dc54a860200d9f1b713c8c.svg) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}2y+6x & 2x-4y \\\\ 2x-4y & -4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6(1) & 2(1)-4(1) \\\\ 2(1)-4(1) & -4(1)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(1)(1)-2(1)^{2}+3(1)^{2}-4 \\\\ (1)^{2}-4(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(8)\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{-36}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{18}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{17}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{18}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205203 :tutorial/content "Recall the example we worked on, where we computed one iteration of the Newton–Raphson method. \n\nWe aim to find a critical point of the function \n\n$$\nf(x,y) =x^2y-2xy^2+x^3-4x,\n$$\n\nin the region $[0,2]\\times[0,2] \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ starting at the point $\\big[ 1, \\: 1 \\big]^T$.\n\nNow, let’s carry out one iteration of Newton–Raphson using linear systems.\n\nThe Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f : \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_{n+1} = \\mathbf{x}_n - [H_f(\\mathbf{x}_n)]^{-1} \\nabla{f}(\\mathbf{x}_n),\n$$\n\nwhere $H_f(\\mathbf{x}_n)$ and $\\nabla{f}(\\mathbf{x}_n)$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at $\\mathbf{x}_n.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\nH_f(\\mathbf{x}_n)(\\mathbf{x}_{n+1} - \\mathbf{x}_n) = -\\nabla{f}(\\mathbf{x}_n).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}-4x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}-4x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4xy\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-4xy) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-4xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2y+6x & 2x-4y \\\\ 2x-4y & -4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n![](images/d6/d6f79b31d5fb338536daa7b8674a68cff04c2e9101987c8d4f81080278c03f17.svg)\n\nStarting with ![](images/57/570a1661bc09970e6fd58e1c4185e37bb113e169052225291eba3757940397b6.svg) we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}2y+6x & 2x-4y \\\\ 2x-4y & -4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2(1)+6(1) & 2(1)-4(1) \\\\ 2(1)-4(1) & -4(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}2(1)(1)-2(1)^{2}+3(1)^{2}-4 \\\\ (1)^{2}-4(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get ![](images/44/44099365d39541bc779228a2411f7a01bec431201cf14850c1e5b33aabe6d74c.svg) Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{18}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{18} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{18}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{17}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{18}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the same result we obtained previously." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204160 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/id #uuid "272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2"] ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/math-academy-id "q-257192"] ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-2,2]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$0.348$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+6 & 8xy-1 \\\\ 8xy-1 & 4{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4x{y}^{2}+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}y-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+6 & 8(-1)(0)-1 \\\\ 8(-1)(0)-1 & 4(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)(0)^{2}+6(-1)-0-2 \\\\ 4(-1)^{2}(0)-(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{23}[\\begin{aligned}-31 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.348 \\\\ 0.087\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674"] ["answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer/id #uuid "fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8"] ["answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8" :answer/value "0.087"] ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/correct "answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8"] ["answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674" :answer-field/choices "answer-fae98102-ed44-578d-91b3-534204bfeae8"] ["question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9ae66afd-66cd-529a-9898-9254316b1674"] [17592186204024 :knowledge-point/questions "question-272bf8c6-2369-5e98-9adb-ebe6db7bece2"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/id #uuid "cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-257191"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-2,0]\\times [-2,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-0.444$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-xy-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy+6x-y-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y+6 & 8x-1 \\\\ 8x-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy+6x-y-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8(-1)+6 & 8(-1)-1 \\\\ 8(-1)-1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}8(-1)(-1)+6(-1)-(-1)-2 \\\\ 4(-1)^{2}-(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 0-(-9)\\cdot (-9)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{81}[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.444 \\\\ -1.012\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4"] ["answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer/id #uuid "0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38"] ["answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38" :answer/value "-1.012"] ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/correct "answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38"] ["answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4" :answer-field/choices "answer-0f6eed4d-3207-5871-b732-3aaed9f76d38"] ["question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b1b8b6be-a31c-573e-bf6e-e966d1666af4"] [17592186204024 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cd16fbf2-f5ff-5242-b610-fb61c79ec2b3"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/id #uuid "08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-257195"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{2}-3xy+2x-{y}^{2}-5)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+6x-3y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3x-2y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+6x-3y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3x-2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+6 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+6x-3y+2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)+6 & 4(-1)-3 \\\\ 4(-1)-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(-1)(-1)+6(-1)-3(-1)+2 \\\\ 2(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-2(-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-2)-(-7)\\cdot (-7)}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{53}[\\begin{aligned}43 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.189 \\\\ -0.340\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29"] ["answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer/id #uuid "734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503"] ["answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503" :answer/value "-0.189"] ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/correct "answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503"] ["answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29" :answer-field/choices "answer-734cf3d0-74b6-5892-a2b6-f02c20d36503"] ["answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf"] ["answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer/id #uuid "c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8"] ["answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8" :answer/value "-0.340"] ["answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/correct "answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8"] ["answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf" :answer-field/choices "answer-c4500310-e39a-50db-8ce7-fa44301d2af8"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c2ba5073-2420-5469-9a7f-592d616a8a29"] ["question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e8aa5d1d-a446-512d-b74d-a1d0ef0175cf"] [17592186204024 :knowledge-point/questions "question-08790f4f-fd5e-5556-9203-49eaf6e8edd8"] [17592186204508 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186204508 :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-8xy-x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-8x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6xy-8x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6y-8 \\\\ 6y-8 & 6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+6x-8y-1 \\\\ 6xy-8x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6(1)-8 \\\\ 6(1)-8 & 6(1)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}+6(1)-8(1)-1 \\\\ 6(1)(1)-8(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 6-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{32}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.125 \\\\ 1.375\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186204508 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer/id #uuid "f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd"] ["answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd" :answer/value "1.125"] [17592186203011 :answer-field/correct "answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd"] [17592186203011 :answer-field/choices "answer-f23445db-e086-52ba-acab-2f3f18598bbd"] ["answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer/id #uuid "6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470"] ["answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470" :answer/value "1.375"] [17592186203012 :answer-field/correct "answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470"] [17592186203012 :answer-field/choices "answer-6cae9a0b-7bb7-5143-a157-fad97fcf5470"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/id #uuid "5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-257198"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[0,\\,1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}+3xy-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}10y-4 & 10x+4y+3 \\\\ 10x+4y+3 & 4x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}10xy-4x+2{y}^{2}+3y \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4xy+3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}10(1)-4 & 10(0)+4(1)+3 \\\\ 10(0)+4(1)+3 & 4(0)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}10(0)(1)-4(0)+2(1)^{2}+3(1) \\\\ 5(0)^{2}+4(0)(1)+3(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 0-7\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ -7 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{49}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -35\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0.286\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/id #uuid "e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759"] ["answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer/id #uuid "358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1"] ["answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1" :answer/value "0.000"] ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/correct "answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1"] ["answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759" :answer-field/choices "answer-358b80c0-d90b-5e9f-b42a-9bff7ca22db1"] ["answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1"] ["answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer/id #uuid "6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812"] ["answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812" :answer/value "0.286"] ["answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/correct "answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812"] ["answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-6fdd4c5d-ae23-5a86-9387-8837df6a1812"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e32003de-1c52-53ff-8dce-b9605e8b1759"] ["question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3689dae0-eb0a-5015-be27-722e43abe4c1"] [17592186204024 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5830491e-19ce-53b6-8fb0-b5e123e740a5"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/id #uuid "7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-257208"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-1,0]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[-0.2,\\,1.2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-3y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2xy-4x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2xy-4x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}-2y-4 & -2x \\\\ -2x & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}-2xy-4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-2(1.2)-4 & -2(-0.2) \\\\ -2(-0.2) & 6(1.2)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-2(-0.2)(1.2)-4(-0.2) \\\\ 3(1.2)^{2}-(-0.2)^{2}-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-6.4 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.4 & 7.2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1.28 \\\\ 1.28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-6.4)\\cdot 7.2-0.4\\cdot 0.4}[\\begin{aligned}7.2 & -0.4 \\\\ -0.4 & -6.4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1.28 \\\\ 1.28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 1.2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{46.24}[\\begin{aligned}8.704 \\\\ -8.704\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-0.012 \\\\ 1.012\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/id #uuid "022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253"] ["answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer/id #uuid "c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a"] ["answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a" :answer/value "-0.012"] ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/correct "answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a"] ["answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253" :answer-field/choices "answer-c922bd52-0c29-5fbc-bcbf-4f7cdd4dc33a"] ["answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa"] ["answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer/id #uuid "b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d"] ["answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d" :answer/value "1.012"] ["answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/correct "answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d"] ["answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-b52d19c7-00d1-561d-b860-e1f24690955d"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-022dd755-e937-5f56-968f-8fdac582d253"] ["question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-940f4f61-0df6-5fbf-92d5-6c0094f915aa"] [17592186204025 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7904745e-3c48-5473-a84d-2ea698eb26ae"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/id #uuid "040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-257222"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}+{y}^{4}-4{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+10)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{3}-8x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{3}-8y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{3}-8x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{y}^{3}-8y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12{y}^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-8x \\\\ 4{y}^{3}-8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}12(2)^{2}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12(2)^{2}-8\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(2)^{3}-8(2) \\\\ 4(2)^{3}-8(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}40 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 40\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{40\\cdot 40-0\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}40 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{1\\,600}[\\begin{aligned}640 \\\\ 640\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.6 \\\\ 1.6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/id #uuid "5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652"] ["answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer/id #uuid "17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1"] ["answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1" :answer/value "1.6"] ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/correct "answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1"] ["answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652" :answer-field/choices "answer-17817482-f3d2-5615-b2cb-6c119b34c2c1"] ["answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7"] ["answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer/id #uuid "19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53"] ["answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53" :answer/value "1.6"] ["answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/correct "answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53"] ["answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7" :answer-field/choices "answer-19d2da55-b35c-5e37-bc82-32d67ef03d53"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5789f198-74e1-5b68-a9ba-3bb1808b8652"] ["question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-862f5751-3521-5986-9159-683bde1d18c7"] [17592186204025 :knowledge-point/questions "question-040d983b-9569-5e20-9386-5dd2354e86bd"] [17592186204506 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [-2,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,-2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2,\\,0]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186204506 :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y+4{x}^{2}-3xy-8x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+8x-3y-8) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+8x-3y-8) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}4y+8 & 4x-3 \\\\ 4x-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}4xy+8x-3y-8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}4(0)+8 & 4(2)-3 \\\\ 4(2)-3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}4(2)(0)+8(2)-3(0)-8 \\\\ 2(2)^{2}-3(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{8\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.6 \\\\ -0.96\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186204506 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer/id #uuid "cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257"] ["answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257" :answer/value "1.600"] [17592186203008 :answer-field/correct "answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257"] [17592186203008 :answer-field/choices "answer-cef5ef8e-8921-513c-9c3a-acdc9d57a257"] ["answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer/id #uuid "c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570"] ["answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570" :answer/value "-0.960"] [17592186203009 :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570"] [17592186203009 :answer-field/choices "answer-c4ffa1c4-2fc8-5122-b761-b9aac580f570"] [17592186204507 :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-6,-3]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[-6,\\,1]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[-3,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$1.75$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186204507 :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}-6x+4{y}^{3}+7)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{y}^{2}-6) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+12{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{2}-6) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+12{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4y \\\\ 4y & 4x+24y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-6 \\\\ 4xy+12{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4(2) \\\\ 4(2) & 4(-3)+24(2)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(2)^{2}-6 \\\\ 4(-3)(2)+12(2)^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 36\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 36-8\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}36 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{64}[\\begin{aligned}-120 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4.875 \\\\ 1.75\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186204507 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer/id #uuid "e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a"] ["answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a" :answer/value "-4.875"] [17592186203010 :answer-field/correct "answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a"] [17592186203010 :answer-field/choices "answer-e7dfbdae-54de-5b55-be97-851277d3ad7a"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/id #uuid "11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/math-academy-id "q-257248"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[2,3]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,2]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[2.25,\\,1.5]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{2}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$1.417$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-6) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6(2.25)-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6(1.5)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3(2.25)^{2}-6(2.25) \\\\ 3(1.5)^{2}-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}7.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{7.5\\cdot 9-0\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7.5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{67.5}[\\begin{aligned}15.1875 \\\\ 5.625\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}2.025 \\\\ 1.417\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853"] ["answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/id #uuid "ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4"] ["answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/value "2.025"] ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/correct "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4"] ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/choices "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4"] ["question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853"] [17592186204025 :knowledge-point/questions "question-11575fd3-3b68-5f5f-9c8d-ffa66ae7367b"] ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/id #uuid "e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91"] ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/math-academy-id "q-257213"] ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [-1,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,-1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-5$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-0.524$\n </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy-2x+3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy-2x+3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10(-1)-2 \\\\ 10(-1)-2 & 10(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}5(-1)^{2}-2(-1)-2(1) \\\\ 10(1)(-1)-2(1)+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 10\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-29/82 \\\\ 39/82\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.646 \\\\ -0.524\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a"] ["answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/id #uuid "a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2"] ["answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/value "-12"] ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/correct "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2"] ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/choices "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2"] ["answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab"] ["answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer/id #uuid "7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f"] ["answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7379b188-4efc-50fd-a5e6-316fc647872f" :answer/value "-12"] ["answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/corre