cc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/id #uuid "5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2"] ["question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-257199"] ["question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,2]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[2,\\,1]^{T}.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$4$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-4$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-2$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}y-4x-2y-2{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-2-4y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-4) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-2-4y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}4xy-4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4(1) & 4(2) \\\\ 4(2) & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}4(2)(1)-4 \\\\ 2(2)^{2}-2-4(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4"] ["answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer/id #uuid "4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec"] ["answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/correct "answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec"] ["answer-field-a16d0722-b98a-5c1d-95f0-119e1fc538e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-4005aa77-18e1-5073-a669-e2b096c350ec"] ["answer-field-f939bf4e-3667-591e-a976-8f0a98ca8d20" :answer-field/id #uuid "f939bf4e-3667-591e-a